/Dest [9 0 R /XYZ 71.982422 629.21014 0]
/Next 1385 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 232 0 R
/SE 240 0 R
/Title (The "No-Cost" Equated Monthly Installment \(EMI\) has emerged as a ubiquitous and powerful marketing tool in the Indian retail and e-commerce landscape, promising consumers the ability to purchase high-value goods without any apparent interest burden. However, this belies the sophisticated financial architecture that underpins these offerings. This paper deconstructs the "no-cost" EMI paradox, revealing it not as a zero-interest facility, but as a complex business model predicated on the strategic distribution of costs and benefits among multiple stakeholders. Through a qualitative analysis of prevailing business models, stakeholder revenue streams, and the regulatory environment, this study addresses how profitability is engineered in the absence of direct interest charges. The findings indicate that profits are generated through a symbiotic ecosystem involving banks and financial institutions, merchants, and product manufacturers. Costs are effectively shifted and shared, manifesting as absorbed discounts for)
>>
endobj
