1400 0 obj
<<
/Dest [236 0 R /XYZ 71.923828 538.53516 0]
/Next 1402 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 1398 0 R
/SE 246 0 R
/Title (However, the term "no-cost" is, in financial reality, a misnomer. The Reserve Bank of India \(RBI\) itself has stated in a 2013 circular that the concept of "zero percent interest is non-existent."[4][5][6] The central bank clarified that in such schemes, the interest element is often camouflaged and passed on to the customer in other forms, such as processing fees.[5][6][7] This regulatory stance did not eliminate these schemes but rather catalyzed their evolution into a more sophisticated, multi-stakeholder model where the interest cost is not waived by the bank but is instead subsidized by other parties in the transaction, primarily the merchant or the manufacturer.[8] This creates a complex financial ecosystem where costs and benefits are intricately distributed, a reality often opaque to the end consumer. )
>>
endobj
