/Prev 1410 0 R
/SE 252 0 R
/Title (The significance of this study is threefold. For consumers, it aims to foster greater financial literacy by revealing the true costs associated with a seemingly free service. For businesses, it provides a strategic analysis of a powerful sales and marketing tool, detailing the symbiotic relationships that make it viable. For policymakers and regulators, it highlights the ongoing need to balance market innovation and consumer protection, particularly concerning transparency in financial products. By deconstructing the "no-cost" EMI model, this paper offers a detailed anatomy of a modern credit mechanism that sits at the intersection of finance, technology, and consumer psychology in one of the world's fastest-growing economies. )
>>
endobj
