/Prev 1414 0 R
/SE 255 0 R
/Title (This study employs a descriptive and analytical research design to deconstruct the "no-cost" EMI ecosystem in India. The methodological approach is primarily qualitative, focusing on synthesizing information from a wide range of secondary sources to build a comprehensive, stakeholder-centric model of profitability. Given the proprietary nature of specific agreements between banks, merchants, and manufacturers, a direct empirical study based on internal corporate data is not feasible. Therefore, this research relies on a meticulous analysis of publicly available information to map the financial flows and strategic incentives that define the system. )
>>
endobj
