/Next 1483 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 1488 0 R
/SE 354 0 R
/Title (As the Indian economy continues its trajectory of growth and digitalization, the role of such innovative credit mechanisms will only expand. The challenge for regulators, financial institutions, and merchants alike will be to foster a market that is not only efficient and profitable but also transparent and fair. Evolving from "no-cost" to "clear-cost" financing may be the necessary next step in ensuring that the credit-fueled growth of today builds a foundation of sustainable and informed financial well-being for the Indian consumer of tomorrow. )
>>
endobj
1487 0 obj
<<
/Count 1
/Dest [15 0 R /XYZ 91.042969 606.8457 0]
/First 1489 0 R
/Last 1489 0 R
/Next 1490 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 1484 0 R
/SE 296 0 R
/Title <>
>>
endobj
1488 0 obj
<<
/Dest [11 0 R /XYZ 71.988281 597.10938 0]
/Next 1486 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 1491 0 R
/SE 353 0 R
/Title (The architecture of this ecosystem has been fundamentally shaped by India's regulatory actions, which transformed "zero-interest" advertising into a compliant subvention system, and by a tax regime that adds a layer of cost. While this model has been a powerful engine for consumption and a catalyst for the growth of the digital finance sector, its defining feature remains a degree of opacity. The term "no-cost" continues to be a marketing illusion that masks the true financial equation from the very consumers it aims to empower. )
>>
endobj
1489 0 obj
<<
/Dest [15 0 R /XYZ 72.169922 548.13379 0]
/Parent 1487 0 R
/SE 297 0 R
/Title (3.3 Profitability Analysis for Merchants and Retailers )
>>
endobj
1490 0 obj
<<
/Dest [15 0 R /XYZ 72.351563 520.60889 0]
/Next 1492 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 1487 0 R
/SE 298 0 R
/Title (For merchants, the cost of subvention is an investment that yields significant returns in sales and market growth. )
>>
endobj
1491 0 obj
<<
/Dest [19 0 R /XYZ 71.988281 98.984375 0]
/Next 1488 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 1493 0 R
/SE 352 0 R
/Title (The "no-cost" EMI is a quintessential example of financial innovation tailored to the specific economic and cultural context of modern India. It is not a scam, but a complex and highly effective business model that redefines profitability by distributing costs across a willing ecosystem of stakeholders. Banks and financial institutions profit through a portfolio of fees, subsidized interest, and expanded credit operations. Merchants and manufacturers willingly absorb interest costs as a strategic marketing expenditure, rewarded with demonstrably higher sales and market penetration. The consumer, in turn, pays for the immense convenience of immediate access and affordability through a series of small, often obscured, costs. )
>>
endobj
