/Title (The results of this analysis paint a clear picture: the "no-cost" EMI scheme in India is a masterfully engineered financial product that thrives on a symbiotic, multi-stakeholder ecosystem. The discussion below synthesizes these findings, explores the regulatory and economic implications, and addresses the critical issues of transparency and consumer welfare. )
>>
endobj
1535 0 obj
<<
/Dest [12 0 R /XYZ 72.287109 491.66162 0]
/Parent 1532 0 R
/SE 331 0 R
/Title (4.3 Broader Economic and Social Implications )
>>
endobj
1536 0 obj
<<
/Dest [14 0 R /XYZ 71.982422 138.881836 0]
/Next 1532 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 1539 0 R
/SE 329 0 R
/Title (The RBI's 2013 circular, which declared that "zero percent interest is non-existent," was a pivotal moment.[5][6][7] Rather than extinguishing EMI schemes, the regulation acted as a catalyst for innovation. It forced the interest component out of the shadows, compelling banks to explicitly charge it. This necessitated the creation of the transparent subvention models seen today, where merchants and manufacturers formally bear the interest cost.[8] The RBI's directive, aimed at preventing the exploitation of "vulnerable customers" through camouflaged interest, paradoxically legitimized a new system where the cost-shifting became the official, compliant mechanism.[4][5][24] The central bank's continuing calls for greater transparency in disclosing the principal, interest, and discounts further reinforce this framework.[18] )
>>
endobj
1537 0 obj
<<
/Dest [14 0 R /XYZ 72.287109 570.81152 0]
/Parent 1534 0 R
/SE 321 0 R
/Title (4.1 An Ecosystem of Interdependent Interests )
>>
endobj
1538 0 obj
<<
/Dest [14 0 R /XYZ 71.923828 543.58496 0]
/Next 1540 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 1534 0 R
/SE 322 0 R
/Title (The sustained success of the "no-cost" EMI model can be attributed to the alignment of interests among its key participants. It is not a zero-sum game but a value-creation cycle where each stakeholder derives a distinct, quantifiable benefit. )
>>
endobj
1539 0 obj
<<
/Dest [14 0 R /XYZ 71.988281 181.93164 0]
/Next 1536 0 R
/Parent 4 0 R
/Prev 1541 0 R
/SE 328 0 R
/Title (The current structure of "no-cost" EMI is a direct consequence of the regulatory environment, shaped primarily by the Reserve Bank of India and the GST regime. )
>>
endobj
1540 0 obj
<<
/Dest [14 0 R /XYZ 91.042969 483.93848 0]
/Next 1542 0 R
